# Manually transcribed by OWID: the share of school children employed in agriculture in 1904, and
# the share of children aged 12-16 working in factories with at least ten workers, from the first
# Reich-wide count of 1874-76 (recorded here under 1875, its mid-point).
# NOTE: the exact pages for these two figures still need to be confirmed.
# In case of updating, upload manually.

# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Kinderarbeit im Kaiserreich 1871-1914"
    description: |-
      A doctoral thesis on child labor in the German Empire, drawing on school surveys and the first Reich-wide factory counts. It reports how many school children worked in agriculture alongside compulsory schooling, and how many children were employed in factories.

      Both measures cover a single sector rather than all of children's work: the 1904 figure counts agricultural work by pupils, and the 1874-76 figure counts only factories employing at least ten workers.
    date_published: "2007"

    # Citation
    producer: Boentert
    citation_full: |-
      Boentert, A. (2007). Kinderarbeit im Kaiserreich 1871-1914. Ferdinand Schöningh, Paderborn.

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.schoeningh.de/
    date_accessed: '2026-09-06'

    # License
    license:
      name: © Boentert (2007)
outs:
